{"results":[{"id":"6ad77e2e717e0153aa2fda49","name":"Active Exploitation of CVE-2026-110936 in Siemens Software Center","description":"A DLL side-loading vulnerability in Software Center version 3.5.8.7 is being actively exploited by attackers. The threat actors distribute a genuine, digitally signed copy of the application alongside malicious DLL files through unofficial channels. When executed, the vulnerable version loads the attacker-supplied DLLs without validation, enabling malicious code execution. The attack vector involves ClickFix social engineering tactics, tricking users into executing commands. The campaign uses specific infrastructure for payload hosting and command-and-control operations. Version 4.0.9.8 patches this vulnerability, with automatic updates applied upon application restart. No official systems or distribution channels were compromised during this campaign.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T14:01:03.768000","created":"2026-10-20T14:43:58.172000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Romulus","indicators":[{"id":4510527974,"indicator":"wizardexpensive.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-20T14:43:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4530811534,"indicator":"CVE-2026-110936","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-20T14:43:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4538071010,"indicator":"3fdcc7d7d049a89711fb31fb236940a1c5a09d899143ffd20c3c41fb1f2cf491","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-20T14:43:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4538071011,"indicator":"f4d7c5321bb0d1bda439304a753bcf9b467b98ca53c7e9493b9c2c3451092e4a","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-20T14:43:58","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["software supply chain","cve-2026-110936","clickfix","industrial software"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1053.005","T1036.005","T1204.002","T1566.002","T1082","T1218.007","T1140","T1083","T1059.001","T1547.001","T1562.001","T1078","T1027","T1486","T1218.010","T1518.001","T1059.003","T1071.001","T1574.002","T1105"],"references":["https:\/\/productcert.siemens.com\/news\/2026\/10\/19\/active-exploitation-of-cve-2026-110936-in-siemens-software-center\/"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afda8f8ad54682e30c1bb10","name":"Behind the Power Outage: Unmasking a New Intrusion Vector in Enterprise Infrastructure Tools","description":"An attacker exploited CyberPower PowerPanel Business (PPB), a UPS management software, to execute malicious code on a Windows domain controller. The threat actor uploaded custom scripts through the web console's file-upload endpoint on TCP port 3052, leveraging PPB's legitimate feature that runs scripts during power events. These scripts executed with SYSTEM privileges through the trusted ppbed.exe service. The attacker downloaded tools using certutil, loaded .NET assemblies into memory, and extracted Active Directory data using ntdsutil and esentutl against ntds.dit. Through iterative script development, the adversary refined their collection process until successful. Finally, they deployed a persistent implant, upnpcont.exe with malicious atl.dll, using DLL side-loading. The operation demonstrated interactive human engagement, utilizing primarily built-in Windows utilities to maintain stealth while compromising critical infrastructure.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T10:49:46.566000","created":"2026-11-18T13:32:40.653000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4590585550,"indicator":"http:\/\/84.200.205.145:55557\/junk50k.bin","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-18T13:32:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["powerpanel business","msil.killav!gen1","active directory extraction","infrastructure software abuse","script injection","system privilege abuse","domain controller compromise","dll side-loading","ups exploitation"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["MSIL.Killav!gen1"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/www.security.com\/threat-intelligence\/power-management-software-attack-vector"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afda8f9f5dd55f9f13c0cd0","name":"GravityRAT Mobile Cyber-Campaign Targets Defense Personnel","description":"An active cyber-surveillance campaign has been uncovered deploying GravityRAT malware against defense industry and military personnel, primarily targeting individuals from India seeking positions at foreign defense contractors. The campaign utilizes fake recruitment portals and software utility websites that mimic legitimate services to distribute malicious payloads. These sites display logos of major defense contractors like Airbus, BAE Systems, Thales, and Lockheed Martin to build credibility. GravityRAT is a multi-platform surveillance framework active since 2015, attributed to Pakistan-aligned threat actors including SpaceCobra and Cosmic Leopard. The malware conducts extensive data exfiltration including contacts, call logs, SMS messages, GPS location, documents, WhatsApp backups, and device identifiers, uploading collected information to command and control servers at regular intervals.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T10:47:55.541000","created":"2026-11-18T13:32:41.172000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"SpaceCobra, Cosmic Leopard, Operation Celestial Force","indicators":[{"id":3357451993,"indicator":"movie-date.net","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-18T13:32:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":3882227827,"indicator":"myvaultz.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-18T13:32:41","content":"","title":"","description":"","expi