title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585545,"indicator":"c2454052f49e43226f69413ce58ba0bb3a2d89e7a52f32ef8adbf0961bb838c2","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585546,"indicator":"c3f6aa4dc9cdbcd2cfdacd18e59e0c1af0406d59d1f81cd962ac3cde60626ee8","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585547,"indicator":"cbd790d052a57d18f1cd58fe4c9887340eec5d38bfae105caf0d222f30a856d5","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585548,"indicator":"d4032e61aa9ef01a5a174a90beffa5a27dd21b36e653ce5304907787554b7d95","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585549,"indicator":"d8ae46604dc4eab411977764bd923af686aea117fb33304520d928f1d382ef0e","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590585550,"indicator":"http:\/\/84.200.205.145:55557\/junk50k.bin","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["privilege escalation","cyberpower powerpanel business","msil.killav!gen1","active directory extraction","infrastructure tools abuse","domain controller compromise","dll side-loading","credential theft","ups exploitation"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["MSIL.Killav!gen1"],"attack_ids":["T1218.011","T1069","T1003.002","T1087.002","T1543.003","T1082","T1140","T1190","T1055","T1112","T1505.003","T1049","T1059.001","T1078","T1027","T1059.003","T1574.002","T1105","T1003.003","T1569.002"],"references":["https:\/\/www.security.com\/blog-post\/power-management-software-attack-vector"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afdaa42ee27fc70ccfe0fad","name":"Bazuka: The Fraud Framework That Can Do It All","description":"In late October 2026, a new mobile threat called Bazuka was discovered while investigating an NFC card relay application. Unlike typical banking trojans with simple architectures, Bazuka is a comprehensive modular framework designed for fraudulent operations. The framework consists of a dropper\/downloader, core component, and 23 specialized modules covering overlays, keylogging, SMS and 2FA interception, remote control, and cryptocurrency address swapping. Notable features include LLM integration within the control panel to help operators manage infections and identify high-value victims, plus ADB bridging capabilities for covert privilege escalation. Distribution occurs through traffers using lures like adult content, with plans for potential Google Play deployment using minimal permissions to bypass review processes. The control panel, partially in Russian, reveals sophisticated victim management tools and AI-assisted targeting capabilities.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T10:44:04.979000","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:10.462000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4480561488,"indicator":"95.181.213.21","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T13:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708011,"indicator":"brokerok.org","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708012,"indicator":"gargona.cash","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708013,"indicator":"c2api.brokerok.org","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708014,"indicator":"c2data.brokerok.org","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708015,"indicator":"c2proxy.brokerok.org","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590708016,"indicator":"c2ws.brokerok.org","type":"hostname","created":"2026-11-18T13:38:11","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["banking trojan","bazuka","llm integration","modular framework","cryptocurrency theft","raton","adb bridging","nfc relay","overlay technique"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["Bazuka","RatOn"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/www.threatfabric.com\/blogs\/bazuka-the-fraud-framework-that-can-do-it-all"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afde5de85d121d01c609834","name":"Open by Default, Already Occupied: Threat Actors are Renting your Compute","description":"Analysis of 11,891 IP addresses reveals that over half of exposed Ollama servers show evidence of unauthorized access. Approximately 65% of affected hosts reside in cloud or hosting networks, with Germany, China, and the United States most impacted. The investigation identified 106,938 model entries across exposed servers, with 24% showing models pulled from raw IP addresses and 22% using free tunneling services. Evidence suggests attackers are exploiting unauthenticated Ollama instances to access paid cloud model subscriptions, conduct server-side request forgery, and attempt path traversal attacks similar to the Probllama vulnerability. Model lists contain Base64-encoded strings targeting sensitive files like \/etc\/shadow and SSH keys, with some malicious artifacts persisting for five months. The exposed infrastructure primarily consists of rental compute resources that lack proper authentication, egress controls, and organizational ownership.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T10:43:07.666000","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30.224000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":3999856959,"indicator":"CVE-2024-37032","type":"CVE","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4058503217,"indicator":"185.165.171.21","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T17:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4466202105,"indicator":"103.249.201.108","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T17:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4471843462,"indicator":"62.31.247.107","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T17:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590805184,"indicator":"http:\/\/103.249.201.108:9882\/trigger\/benign:latest","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4590805185,"indicator":"http:\/\/trycloudflare.com\/read\/x5fa4534:b1","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-18T17:52:30","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["path-traversal","rental-compute","cloud-models","ollama","llmjacking","embedding-models","cve-2024-37032","unauthenticated-api","ssrf"],"targeted_countries":["United States of America","China","Germany"],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":["T1033","T1133","T1071.004","T1552.005","T1087.001","T1530","T1082","T1071","T1005","T1190","T1552","T1572","T1016","T1087","T1090","T1083","T1102","T1552.001","T1078","T1071.001","T1018","T1078.004"],"references":["https:\/\/www.rapid7.com\/blog\/post\/tr-self-hosted-ai-renting-compute-exposed-servers"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6afe21487f55b1567b331b59","name":"Fake FMCSA, DAT, and TIMOCOM Portals: 3 Cyberattacks Targeting US Logistics","description":"Three distinct campaigns are actively targeting American trucking and logistics companies through digital platforms used for routine business operations. HelloFriends employs fraudulent carrier verification portals impersonating SAFER and Motus to harvest credentials, personal identification data, and fuel card information via sophisticated phishing infrastructure. NodeRemote distributes malware through fake broker documents and onboarding pages, deploying Node.js backdoors with rotating command-and-control infrastructure that maintains persistent remote access to compromised endpoints. The Fake Freight Portals campaign impersonates TIMOCOM and DAT, using malicious WebDAV shortcuts to install MeshCentral and CastleRAT remote access tools, while attempting to extract BitLocker recovery keys and weakening endpoint defenses. These campaigns exploit familiar business workflows including carrier verification, broker onboarding, and freight booking to compromise operational systems and sensitive business data.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-19T10:42:33.398000","created":"2026-11-18T22:06:00.520000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4510423918,"indicator":"87.120.104.213","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-18T22:06:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-18T22:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4557241616,"indicator":"925a9d35a32e1a6a1ce1ae4b9ff09e289184d4d925d700752c99f15ab04296dd","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-18T22:06:01","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4559141796,"indicator":"f74a0fbddac01f282b070fc6b57811a6","type":"FileHash-MD5","created"